Theorem RL-16: escaping heap allocation (Locality >= HeapEscaping)

  Preconditions:
    - RL-16 governs escaping heap allocation per Annex E §AIMS Stack
      Promotion: escaping values (Locality >= HeapEscaping) SHALL be
      heap-allocated with a full RC header.
    - Signature ArcFunction x AimsStateMap -> ArcFunction per
      the canonical proof notation:264; discharged against the sec-01
      Realization.proof sorry obligation.
    - DP-8 (is_local) is false for HeapEscaping and Unknown — these are the
      non-promotable localities; the stack-promotion rules (RL-14 / RL-14a /
      RL-15) and the caller-stack rule (RL-15a, ArgEscaping) do not apply.
    - Shipped: realize/decide.rs Locality consumption; repr.md sec-RH-3
      (escaping values carry an RC header).
    - depends-on sec-05: DP-8 (is_local).

  Soundness property:
    Forall value v with Locality(v) >= HeapEscaping:

      (P1) Strategy decision: RL-16 selects a heap allocation with a full RC
           header, regardless of Uniqueness or size.

      (P2) Lifetime soundness: a value that escapes its function frame
           (HeapEscaping) or whose escape is Unknown cannot live on the stack
           — the stack frame is popped on return, leaving a stack value
           dangling. A heap allocation with a full RC header tracks the
           value's (possibly shared, possibly multi-frame) lifetime correctly,
           freeing it when the count reaches zero.

    RL-16 is the conservative fallback of the Locality lattice: any value the
    analysis cannot prove non-escaping (or proves heap-escaping) gets the
    full heap + RC-header treatment — the same as plain ARC, since no
    refinement is provable.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by the case_analysis engine via exhaustive
    enumeration of the escaping localities x Uniqueness x size.

    Part (P1/P2) — escaping strategy grid:
      The verifier asserts every (HeapEscaping / Unknown) x (Unique /
      MaybeShared / Shared) x (fixed / dynamic) combination selects Heap.
      Coverage gate: 12 combinations. Negative-direction witness: a
      heap-escaping value must NOT be stack-promoted (headerless / immortal /
      bump) — it would dangle after the frame is popped — asserted.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — section_08::verify_rl16_escaping_heap;
        escaping-locality strategy enumeration; emits Fail on a wrong
        strategy or a stack-promotion of an escaping value)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_08 case_analysis engine discharges RL-16 via exhaustive enumeration of escaping localities (HeapEscaping / Unknown) x Uniqueness x size -> heap allocation with a full RC header, with a negative-direction witness rejecting stack promotion of a heap-escaping value, grounded in repr.md RH-3 + realize/decide.rs Locality consumption
